Line 1: A list inside a list needs parentheses.
    let rows be a list of a list of 1 and 2, and a list of 3
                            ^^^^^^^
Write it like "a list of (a list of 1 and 2) and (a list of 3 and 4)".

Line 2: A position worked out with arithmetic needs parentheses.
    say item n plus 1 of scores
               ^^^^
Write it like "item (n plus 1) of scores".

Line 3: Something is missing after "item".
    say item of scores
        ^^^^
Say which item, like "item 1", "the first item", or "the last item".

Line 4: Something is missing after "item".
    remove item from scores
           ^^^^
Say which item, like "item 1", "the first item", or "the last item".

Line 5: "every" has to start the value, because everything after it is worked out for each item.
    say 2 plus every n in scores
               ^^^^^
Put it in parentheses, like "(every score in scores plus 5)".

Line 6: I expected a comparison like "are at least" here, but found "70".
    say only the scores that 70
                             ^^
Write it like "only the scores that are at least 70".

Line 7: With "by their length", say "longest first" or "shortest first".
    sort names by their length, biggest first
                                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^

Line 8: "longest first" sorts by length, so it needs "by their length".
    sort names, longest first
                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Write it like "sort names by their length, longest first".

Line 9: I expected "from" here, but found "scores".
    remove the first item scores
                          ^^^^^^
Write it like "remove item 2 from scores".

Line 10: Something is missing after "insert".
    insert at position 1 of scores
    ^^^^^^
Add a value there, like a number, some text in quotes, or a name.

Line 11: Comparisons can't be chained like this.
    say scores is empty is yes
                        ^^
Compare one pair at a time and join them with "and".

Line 12: I don't know the kind of value "number".
    let kinds be an empty list of number
                                  ^^^^^^
Lists and maps hold "numbers", "text", "yes/no values", "lists of" something, or "maps from" something, like "a list of numbers".

Line 13: EasyScript doesn't have "are not above".
    say only the scores that are not above 3
                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Did you mean "are at most"?

Line 14: "are above or equal to" isn't a comparison.
    say only the scores that are above or equal to 3
                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Did you mean "are at least"?

Line 15: I don't know the kind of value "banana".
    to f with x (a list of banana):
                           ^^^^^^
Lists and maps hold "numbers", "text", "yes/no values", "lists of" something, or "maps from" something, like "a list of numbers".

Line 17: Something is missing after "list of".
    to g with y (a list of):
                   ^^^^^^^
Say what the list holds, like "a list of numbers".

Line 20: "longest first" sorts by length, so it needs "by their length".
    say n sorted longest first
                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Write it like "names sorted by their length longest first".

Line 21: With "by their length", say "longest first" or "shortest first".
    say n sorted by their length biggest first
                                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^

Line 22: Something is missing after "sorted biggest".
    say n sorted biggest
          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Did you mean "sorted biggest first"?
